      "source": "Marker for the First Jewish Site in Los Angeles County",
      "description": "\"First Jewish site in Los Angeles\" — first organized  Jewish community effort in Los Angeles, acquiring a cemetery site from the city in 1855.\nThe Hebrew Benevolent Society Cemetery was located at Lookout Drive and Lilac Terrace, in Chavez Ravine, central Los Angeles. Circa 1890s the bodies were moved to the Home of Peace Cemetery in East Los Angeles.\nPresent day historical marker located south of Dodger Stadium, behind the police academy, in the Elysian Park area.",
